.page comm 1 compare two sorted files line by line

# SYNOPSIS
*comm* [*-123*] _FILE1_ _FILE2_

# DESCRIPTION
`comm` reads two files that are already sorted and writes three columns: lines only in _FILE1_, lines only in _FILE2_, and lines in both. The columns are separated by tabs. A file name of `-` means standard input.

# OPTIONS
@ *-1*
    Leave out the first column.
@ *-2*
    Leave out the second column.
@ *-3*
    Leave out the third column.

# EXAMPLES
    comm -12 a.txt b.txt
    comm -3 old.txt new.txt

# SEE ALSO
sort(1), uniq(1), cmp(1)
